Your pushes are now end-to-end encrypted: only devices you sign in on can read them. Signing in shows a recovery key. Save it: it is the only way back to your pushes if you forget your password. Change password and Show a new recovery key are in the menu.

A link's icon now comes from its page and travels with the push, so your list never asks Google. Older links show a plain icon. Notifications and search work on encrypted pushes, and an unconfirmed share is retried, not dropped.
